<title>FINLAND: TAMPELLA RULED TO PAY $10 MLN COMPENSATION.</title>
<headline>TAMPELLA RULED TO PAY $10 MLN COMPENSATION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Tampella Oy, controlled by Swedish Sandvik Ab , said a U.S. court had ruled a $10.2 million compensation to be paid by its U.S. subsidiary Driltech Inc in a patent dispute.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite this Tampella group's result for the final four months of 1996 is expected to be positive,&quot; it said in a statement, adding Driltech intended to appeal the ruling.  </p>
<p>The company, which is changing its name to Tamrock, said the decision did not apply to possible legal fees or punitive demages: the court would rule on these matters in the next few months.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0247</p>
</text>
